# Projects
rumc-project-title = Projects with the outside
rumc-project-hint = Pick a faction or a city, then a project. The price is paid once, and then the project works; an embassy costs money every minute.
rumc-project-factions = Factions
rumc-project-cities = Cities of the map
rumc-project-target-faction = { $name } (attitude { $value })
rumc-project-target-city = { $name } (attitude { $value })
rumc-project-needs-faction = A faction is needed.
rumc-project-needs-city = A city is needed.
rumc-project-active = Projects at work: { $used } of { $max }
rumc-project-active-none = There are no projects.
rumc-project-active-line = { $name }: { $target }
rumc-project-permanent = no end
rumc-project-left = { $time } left
rumc-project-close = Close the project
rumc-project-cost = Cost { $cost }, keeping { $upkeep } a minute, term: { $time }
rumc-project-start = Begin
rumc-project-blocked-many = { $max } projects at work already.
rumc-project-blocked-active = Such a project with this side goes already.
rumc-project-blocked-money = The budget has not enough money.
rumc-project-blocked-target = A fitting side is needed.
rumc-project-blocked-relation = The attitude must be { $value }.
rumc-project-embassy-name = Permanent embassy
rumc-project-embassy-desc = The city opens an embassy at a faction. It costs to keep, but the ambassador gets points of influence and the faction thinks the better of the city.
rumc-project-mission-name = Trade mission
rumc-project-mission-desc = The city sends a mission to another city. Money to the budget and better attitude while it works.
rumc-project-caravan-name = Caravan way
rumc-project-caravan-desc = A standing way of the caravans to a trade hub. A good income and a cheaper duty.
rumc-project-arms-route-name = Arms route
rumc-project-arms-route-desc = Supplies from the arms city. The calls of the third parties are cheaper, and a little income.

# The grey business
rumc-covert-title = Grey business
rumc-covert-hint = Dear, with a chance of failure. The better the city is known for such things, the worse it goes. When it is too plain, it breaks out into a scandal and every faction thinks the worse of the city. Only the mayor knows what came of it.
rumc-covert-heat = How well known: { $value } of 100
rumc-covert-cost = Cost { $cost }, chance { $chance }%
rumc-covert-effects = Success: { $success }. Failure: { $failure }. Heat +{ $heat }.
rumc-covert-run = Pull it off
rumc-covert-blocked-cooldown = Not again at once: { $seconds } s.
rumc-covert-blocked-money = The budget has not enough money.
rumc-covert-out-reward = money { $sum }
rumc-covert-out-fine = money lost { $sum }
rumc-covert-out-attitude = what the faction thinks { $value }
rumc-covert-out-relation = what the city thinks { $value }
rumc-covert-out-points = points of influence to the ambassador { $value }
rumc-covert-log = What was done
rumc-covert-log-none = No grey affairs yet.
rumc-covert-log-success = Done: { $name } ({ $target }). { $outcome }
rumc-covert-log-failure = Failed: { $name } ({ $target }). { $outcome }
rumc-covert-spy-name = Agent intelligence
rumc-covert-spy-desc = Buy news of a faction and sell it again. Money almost for certain, but a failure spoils the relations.
rumc-covert-bribe-name = Bribe an ambassador
rumc-covert-bribe-desc = Pay the ambassador of a faction for a good word. Success much improves the attitude, failure hits it and the budget.
rumc-covert-pressure-name = Pressure on a faction
rumc-covert-pressure-desc = Squeeze money out of a faction with threats. Much money, but the attitude is spoiled even when it works.
rumc-covert-city-intel-name = Intelligence in a city
rumc-covert-city-intel-desc = Gather news of another city of the map and sell it. If it fails, the city is offended.
rumc-covert-black-deal-name = Shadow deal
rumc-covert-black-deal-desc = Trade round the duty. No target is needed, the chance is high, but a failure costs dear.
